Running the code on vscode:

-Open vscode, Create a new folder.
-Install Python 3.10 (from the web) and tick \'93Add Python to PATH\'94 during installation.
-IN the terminal in vscode, run
	>> pip install \'94numpy<2\'94 opencv-python==4.10.0.84 mediapipe==0.10.14 pyserial
-Run the code.


Debugging on blender:

Paste the code from \'93blender.py\'94 into blender.
Open blender, go to the \'93Scripting\'94 tab in blender.

Press "new+" and paste the code there.
Press run in blender and then run "hand_tracker.py" in vscode.
A rigged hand will appear in blender which moves as per the camera feed from vscode.
Make sure to enable port listening between apps on device.
